    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d829">

                <pb facs="1241" n="1225" xml:id="pg1225"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/7–1349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Israel
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-13T19:00:00-04:00">July 13, 1949—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">
                        niact
                    </hi>
                </p>
                <p>446. Follows message from Bunche to Sharett, Jul 13, concerning final phase
                    Syrian-Israeli armistice negotiations:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text of Mr. Bunche’s message to Israeli Foreign Minister
                    Sharett. It noted that the Syrians had accepted the fundamental Israeli
                    condition that they withdraw from their occupied positions in Palestine, subject
                    to three conditions. Mr. Bunche requested that Mr. Sharett go as far as he
                    reasonably could toward accepting the Syrian reservations, in order to conclude
                    speedily the prolonged negotiations.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d829-f1"/>]</p>
                <p>Dept desires you see Sharett soonest and give full support to position set out in
                    Bunche message, emphasizing earnest hope US Govt that remaining obstacles
                    conclusion armistice can be surmounted. You may wish first consult with Riley
                    and Vigier in order obtain additional background remaining points at issue.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d829-f1" n="1" xml:id="d829-f1-content">
                <p>The text of Mr. Bunche’s message was sent to the Department by New York in
                    telegram 827, July 13, 10:51 p. m., 501.BB Palestine/7–4349. Ambassador Austin,
                    the same day, reported Mr. Bunche’s observation that “he would be ‘greatly
                    obliged if Department of ‘State could get across to Tel Aviv’ support for his
                    representations to Sharett” (telegram 824 from New York, 501.BB
                    Palestine/7–1349).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
